  "goodToKnow": "Der Städter (die Städterin) is a city dweller or townie: der Großstädter, gestresste Städter. Country people may say it slightly mockingly. The opposite is der Landbewohner or der Dörfler. About three quarters of Germans live in towns and cities, but unlike many countries, Germany has no single dominant metropolis. Die Stadt means town or city. The plural is the same."
